### Empty body - all required fields missing
# @name EmptyBody
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Invalid e-mail
# @name InvalidEmail
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Ing.",
    "name": "Jan",
    "surname": "Novak",
    "phone": "+421900111222",
    "email": "not-an-email"
}

### Name contains digits
# @name InvalidName
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Ing.",
    "name": "J0hn",
    "surname": "Novak",
    "phone": "+421900111222",
    "email": "john@example.com"
}

### Phone contains letters
# @name InvalidPhone
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Ing.",
    "name": "Jan",
    "surname": "Novak",
    "phone": "abc",
    "email": "jan@example.com"
}

### Phone too long (16 characters)
# @name TooLongPhone
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Ing.",
    "name": "Jan",
    "surname": "Novak",
    "phone": "1234567890123456",
    "email": "jan@example.com"
}

### Degree too long (11 characters)
# @name TooLongDegree
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST http://localhost:5080/api/employees/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Ingenieurka",
    "name": "Jan",
    "surname": "Novak",
    "phone": "+421900111222",
    "email": "jan@example.com"
}

### Update with invalid data
# @name UpdateInvalid
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
PUT http://localhost:5080/api/employees/{{EmployeeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Ing.",
    "name": "",
    "surname": "Novak",
    "phone": "+421900111222",
    "email": "jan.novak@example.com"
}

### Get non-existing employee
# @name GetUnknown
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
GET http://localhost:5080/api/employees/999999
Accept: application/json

### Update non-existing employee
# @name UpdateUnknown
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
PUT http://localhost:5080/api/employees/999999
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "degree": "Ing.",
    "name": "Jan",
    "surname": "Novak",
    "phone": "+421900111222",
    "email": "jan@example.com"
}
